---
import Layout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Lottie from '../../components/Lottie.astro';

const meta = {
  title: "Helping eztrackr scale with a collaborative design system  — ysabella nicole alvarez",
  description: "Ysabella built a design system and clear, scalable workspace to streamline cross-team collaboration for Eztrackr, a web-based dashboard helping job hunters keep track of their applications all in one place.",
  ogImage: '/opengraph.png'  
}

const src = "https://assets.ysabella.me/cdn-cgi/image/format=webp,quality=100,width=1280";
const raw = "https://assets.ysabella.me"

const data = {
  status: 'roadmap' as const,
  headline: "Building consistency through a design system and better cross-team collaboration.",
  subline: "Eztrackr is a kanban-style web application for tracking job opportunities built on comprehensive, data-intensive dashboards. My task was to establish a clear workspace structure and design system to ease development handoff and maintain consistency as the platform grows.",
  cover: {
    type: 'image' as const,
    src: `${src}/work/eztrackr/banner.png`,
    alt: "Desktop dashboard for Eztrackr, a tracking board for job hunters tracking their applications. The dashboard is focused on a resume, with a tab bar currently displaying the following tabs: Personal Details, Education, Professional Summary, Experience Skills, and More. Currently on the Experience tab, the user has the option to fill in and reorganize their work experience or select a toggle to sort by date."
  },
  details: [
    { label: "Product", value: "Web dashboard application" },
    { label: "Role", value: "Product designer" },
    { label: "Timeline", value: ["July 2025 -", "August 2025"]},
    { label: "Contribution", value: ["Product design", "Design system", "Workflow optimization"] }
  ],
  subheadings: [
    { depth: 2, text: "problem", slug: "problem" },
    { depth: 2, text: "solution", slug: "solution" },
    { depth: 2, text: "reflections", slug: "reflections" }
  ]
}
---
<Layout metadata={meta} data={data} >
  <section class="column sm" id="problem">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Problem</h3>
          <h2 class="title">How do we maintain consistency across a growing interface?</h2>
      </header>
      <p>Eztrackr spans dozens of user flows and hundreds of components, with more continuously being added. With a small design and engineering team and new features launching rapidly, not having a unified design system in place meant the risk of visual drift and confusion during handoff.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="card lg stretch">
      <Lottie 
        src=`${raw}/work/eztrackr/problem.json`
        darkSrc=`${raw}/work/eztrackr/problem-dark.json`
        loop={true}
        autoplay={true}
      />
      <figcaption class="caption horizontal center">My interpretation of lack of structure.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="column lg" id="solution">
    <div class="column xs">
      <header>
         <h3 class="caption label">Solution</h3>
          <h2 class="title">A scalable design system built to support growth.</h2>
      </header>
      <p>My focus was on establishing structure early. To create a product that could scale without friction, I started with the foundational building blocks, ensuring everything from typographic scale to color tokens was properly defined.</p>
      <p>Essentially, I focused on a few key areas that would have the most impact:</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="card lg stretch">
      <div class="stack column md">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Screens</div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Components</div>
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Patterns</div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Spacing</div>
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Typography</div>
          <div class="card lg block caption label vertical center">Colors</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="caption horizontal center">Building blocks of a design system.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="row lg wrap start">
      <div class="card lg vertical stretch">
        <h4>Style guidelines.</h4>
        <p>I defined typography styles and hundreds of color tokens to reduce duplication and inconsistencies.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card lg vertical stretch">
        <h4>Work structure.</h4>
        <p>I grouped flows and screens by status to make progress visible, clarify ownership, and improve developer handoff.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card lg vertical stretch">
        <h4>Responsiveness.</h4>
        <p>I adapted comprehensive dashboards to mobile, with hierarchy and legibility preserved on smaller screens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column xs">
      <p>By investing early in a strong design system along with a clear workspace structure, the team was able to scale a complex product without losing clarity or momentum. With these foundations in place, features like theming become straightforward and a matter of adding instead of fully refactoring.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card lg note" id="reflections">
    <h3 class="caption label">Reflections</h3>
    <div class="row start wrap lg">
      <div class="column xs">
        <h4>Set standards early.</h4>
        <p class="subtle">I’ve found it helps to build a standard set of tokens and components as a reusable foundation. From there, it’s only a matter of adapting them to each new project.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="column xs">
        <h4>When in doubt, get help.</h4>
        <p class="subtle">Things can slip through the cracks. Figma’s color selection, scripts, and third-party plugins came in handy for tracking down raw values and standardizing them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .stack {
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .stack .row {
    width: 100%;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .block {
    display: flex;
    flex-basis: 30%;
    background-color: var(--color-background-300);
  }
</style>